# The sandbox's file. @ai-hero/sandcastle reads it as
# `<repo>/.sandcastle/.env` — the path is hardcoded in the library, which is why
# this file keeps the unhelpful name — and forwards **every key listed here** into
# the container, taking the host's value for a key left blank.
#
# So this is a declaration of what the agent gets to see. Nothing host-side goes
# here: tracker credentials, Slack and Watchtower live in .sandcastle/host.env,
# and env.ts refuses to start the watcher if one of them turns up in this
# file. See docs/adr/0009-two-env-files-one-for-each-side.md.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in — the real file is gitignored.

# Claude Code OAuth token — get one by running `claude setup-token` on your host.
# Lets the agent use your Claude subscription instead of an API key.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key instead — uncomment and fill in:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# GitHub Packages token for @finstreet/* — the repo's .npmrc expands ${NPM_AUTH_TOKEN}
# and `pnpm install` in the container 401s without it. Needs `read:packages`.
# May be left empty: sandcastle forwards a key listed here but falls back to the
# host's value when it is blank, so the token can stay in ~/.zshrc. Fill it in if you
# ever run the watcher from a shell that does not export it (launchd, cron, CI).
NPM_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Bearer token for finstreet-mcp, the SSE server bundled with the
# finstreet-fe@finstreet-plugins plugin that .claude/settings.json enables. The plugin's
# .mcp.json expands ${FINSTREET_MCP_TOKEN} into an Authorization header; without it the
# server is configured but never connects, which looks exactly like an agent that ignored
# its tools. The URL has a default in the plugin, so no FINSTREET_MCP_URL key is needed
# unless you point the sandbox at a non-production server.
# May be left empty, same as NPM_AUTH_TOKEN above.
FINSTREET_MCP_TOKEN=
